      "description": "Watch Bayer Leverkusen vs Union Berlin highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 5, 2026. The Bundesliga clash at the BayArena on 2026-09-05 set the stage for a tactical battle between Bayer Leverkusen and Union Berlin . Fans expected a tightly contested match as both sides looked to secure vital points in their early-season campaign. Lightning Start for the Hosts Bayer Leverkusen wasted no time in making their presence felt, scoring in the very first minute of the match. A slick passing move involving Malik Tillman and Miguel Gutierrez resulted in Equi Fernandez tapping the ball home for an early lead. The hosts continued to apply relentless pressure, and their dominance paid off again in the 28th minute. Facundo Medina rose highest to meet an Aleix Garcia corner, powering a header into the net to double the advantage. Union Berlin struggled to find their rhythm under the sun, with Felix Uduokhai picking up an early yellow card for a rough challenge. Despite their efforts to catch the Leverkusen defense off-guard, several offside calls against Emmanuel Latte Lath prevented the visitors from mounting a serious threat before the break. Leverkusen Extend Their Lead Any hopes of a Union Berlin comeback were dashed shortly after the restart. In the 48th minute, Patrik Schick found himself in space after a delivery from Jarell Quansah and finished clinically with his left foot. Leverkusen’s control of the game was absolute, maintaining 65% possession and restricting the visitors to rare counter-attacking opportunities. The scoring was completed in the 66th minute when Ibrahim Maza unleashed a stunning strike from outside the box. Assisted by Patrik Schick , Maza’s right-footed effort left Frederik Roennow with no chance, effectively ending the contest as a spectacle. Professional Finish As the clock wound down, the Bayer Leverkusen management utilized their bench, introducing Lucas Vazquez and Robert Andrich to maintain the team's energy. Union Berlin also made several tactical substitutions, including Christopher Trimmel and Tim Skarke , but the hosts remained disciplined. Even a late yellow card for Ibrahim Maza for kicking the ball away couldn't dampen the spirits of the home crowd. The final whistle confirmed a thoroughly deserved victory for a clinical Bayer Leverkusen side."
